values ('brand-architecture', 'Brand Architecture', 'Brand & Identity', 'How a company organises its brands, sub-brands and products so growth adds clarity instead of confusion.', 'Every company eventually has more than one thing to name — a new range, a new market, a new venue. Brand architecture is the decision system that determines what gets its own name, what borrows the parent’s, and how the whole family stays legible as it grows.', ARRAY['Portfolio and structure audit', 'Master-brand vs sub-brand decisions', 'Naming and nomenclature rules', 'Roll-out governance']::text[], 'When we launch the next thing, does it strengthen us or dilute us?', 'A structure that scales without a rename every eighteen months.', ARRAY['brand architecture strategy', 'sub brand vs master brand', 'brand portfolio strategy', 'how to name a product line']::text[], 3, true)
